Input fixtures for the installed-binary E2E cases (tests/e2e/cases/*.cmake).

Reference them from a case as `STDIN <file>` (resolved relative to this directory) or as
`{{INPUTS}}/<file>` inside ARGS or ENV values. Keep fixtures small, deterministic and free of real
data, credentials or personal paths: they are committed, and goldens may echo them.

This file itself doubles as a committed regular file (for example a DIR argument that is a file).


Title lists for `mangadex-dl batch` (batch/)
============================================

The CSV lists the `batch` cases read (tests/e2e/cases/batch.cmake and the `batch-*` cases in
_edge.cmake), as FILE (`{{INPUTS}}/batch/<name>.csv`) or on stdin (`STDIN batch/<name>.csv`). The ids
are the fixture ids below. They are byte-exact test data: .gitattributes marks `batch/*.csv -text`, so
git never rewrites their line ends, and batch.cmake fails the configure if excel.csv loses its BOM or
its CRLF. Write or change them with `printf` (never an editor that may convert line ends), then
check the bytes with `od -c`.

  clean.csv                 headerless: 1111... (one title)
  bulk.csv                  headerless: 3333... (the bulk tree, for the SIGPIPE cases)
  incomplete.csv            headerless: 4444...
  clean-unknown.csv         headerless: 1111..., 6666... (row 2 is not found)
  nochapters-mixed.csv      headerless: 5555..., 6666... (exit 5 then 4 on the nochapters tree)
  nochapters-fail-fast.csv  the same two rows, for the --fail-fast cases
  two-clean.csv             headerless: 1111... twice (row 2 is a duplicate)
  four-clean.csv            headerless: 1111..., 2222..., 3333..., 4444... (four distinct rows, for
                            the network-failure streak)
  comments-only.csv         only `#` comments and a blank line (an empty list)
  row-dir.csv               `manga,dir`: 1111...,series/clean
  row-dir-file.csv          `manga,dir`: 1111...,README/x and 1111..., (empty dir). With DIR
                            {{INPUTS}}, row 1's dir runs into this README, a regular file
  unknown-dir.csv           `manga,dir`: 6666...,sub (not found; must leave no directory behind)
  dir-escape.csv            `manga,dir`: 1111...,../x (rejected: escapes DIR)
  dir-absolute.csv          `manga,dir`: 1111...,/abs (rejected: absolute)
  excel.csv                 UTF-8 BOM + CRLF: `manga,title` / 1111...,"Excel, Title"
  excel-bad.csv             UTF-8 BOM + CRLF: a good row on line 2, then an unterminated quote that
                            starts on line 3
  invalid-utf8.csv          the byte 0xFF on line 1
  chapter-url.csv           headerless: a chapter URL on line 1, then 1111... (not a title, not a
                            column)


Generated MangaDex fixtures ({{FIXTURES}})
==========================================

The MangaDex data is NOT committed. The `e2e.fixtures` CTest fixture (FIXTURES_SETUP e2e_fixtures,
required by every cli_e2e_case) runs the test-only `mangadex_dl_fixture_gen <build>/e2e-fixtures`
(tests/e2e/fixtures/fixture_gen.cpp), which writes five trees from the canned fixtures in
tests/support/mdx_fixture.hpp, replacing any previous copy:

  {{FIXTURES}}/clean        11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111  "Clean Title": vol 1 (ch 1-2),
                            vol 2 (ch 3), en, one group, PNG/GIF pages, a cover per volume; no skips,
                            no warnings
  {{FIXTURES}}/basic        22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222  "Basic Title": two groups (dedupe),
                            loose ch 10 and 10.5, a oneshot, an external chapter, pages == 0, an
                            isUnavailable chapter, an fr chapter, JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP pages, covers with
                            volume null and locale null
  {{FIXTURES}}/bulk         33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  4000 loose en chapters with a long
                            title and no images: for dry runs (well over 128 KiB of output)
  {{FIXTURES}}/incomplete   44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444  vol 1 complete; vol 2 lists a page
                            whose file is missing
  {{FIXTURES}}/nochapters   55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555555  only de chapters

Point the tool at one with `--api-base file://{{FIXTURES}}/<name>`. Any other manga id (for example
66666666-6666-4666-8666-666666666666) has no manga document, so it is a 404 (not found).

Layout of one tree (<root> = {{FIXTURES}}/<name>), matching the fixture transport's URL mapping:

  <root>/api/manga/<mangaId>.json                    GET /manga/<id>?includes[]=...
  <root>/api/manga/<mangaId>/feed/offset-<n>.json    GET /manga/<id>/feed?...&offset=<n>
                                                     (n = 0, 500, 1000, ...; offset-0 always exists)
  <root>/api/cover/offset-<n>.json                   GET /cover?manga[]=<id>&limit=100&offset=<n>
                                                     (n = 0, 100, ...; offset-0 always exists)
  <root>/api/at-home/server/<chapterId>.json         GET /at-home/server/<chapterId>
  <root>/uploads/covers/<mangaId>/<fileName>         cover images
  <root>/at-home/data/<hash>/<file>                  page images ({baseUrl}/data/<hash>/<file>)
  <root>/at-home/data-saver/<hash>/<file>            the same bytes ({baseUrl}/data-saver/...)

Rules the fixtures follow (and tests may rely on):
- JSON shapes are MangaDex's (docs/design/download-factcheck.md, cluster F), with a few extra fields
  parsers must ignore. Feed pages hold EVERY language: fixture mode ignores the query string except
  `offset`, so the client filters by language itself.
- Every at-home `baseUrl` is `https://fixture.invalid`. Page names are p001.<ext>, ... (data) and
  s001.<ext>, ... (data-saver).
- A chapter without images has no at-home document (a 404). A "missing" page is listed in the
  at-home document but has no file (a 404 at fetch time).
- PNG and GIF images are real and decodable. JPEG and WebP images are header-only: sniffable (JPEG
  SOF0, WebP VP8X) but not decodable.
- Ids, hashes and file names match ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$. Titles never contain '[', ']' or
  ';' (the CMake driver cannot pass them in file assertions).
